# Copy to .env for local development, or set these where the site is built.
# .env is gitignored. Both are public by design — they are visible in the
# markup of every deployed page — which is why they are here and the Worker's
# secrets are not (see .dev.vars.example for those).
#
# Unlike a Worker secret, these are read at build time: a build without them
# produces pages without them, and setting them afterwards changes nothing
# until the site is rebuilt.

# The Turnstile site key the Hire page's widget renders with (issue #10).
# Unset, the build falls back to Cloudflare's always-pass test key, whose
# dummy token the real secret rejects — so the form fails closed rather than
# letting unverified inquiries through. See src/lib/turnstile.ts.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# The Cloudflare Web Analytics site token (issue #14,
# docs/adr/0002-cloudflare-web-analytics.md). Created in the Cloudflare
# dashboard under Web Analytics, per site. Unset, the build carries no beacon
# and reports nothing anywhere.
PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=
